# VTID-03944 — commands actually run.

# --- Investigation ---------------------------------------------------------

# Reported live: "why is the operator popup screen flickering??? its annoying"

grep -n "isOperatorOpen" services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/app.js
#   -> found existing prior-art: VTID-0526-E (SSE ticker gate) and VTID-03906
#      (_actionRequiredTimer gate) already fixed this exact bug class once
#      each. Both comments explicitly describe "a background poller tearing
#      down and rebuilding the whole DOM ... unprompted."

grep -n "setInterval" services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/app.js
#   -> enumerated every setInterval in the file (11 call sites), read the
#      body of each to see which ones call renderApp() (directly or via a
#      fetch-then-render function) without checking state.isOperatorOpen.

# Confirmed 4 more unguarded instances, none checking state.isOperatorOpen:
#   1. state.executionStatusPollInterval (5s)  -> fetchExecutionStatus() -> renderApp()
#   2. state.devAutopilot.pollerId (10s)       -> fetchDevAutopilotState() -> renderApp()
#   3. state.autonomyPulse.pollerId (30s)      -> fetchAutonomyPulse() -> renderApp()
#   4. state.autonomyTrace.pollerId (30s)      -> fetchAutonomyTrace() -> renderApp()
# Each is gated only on unrelated conditions (selectedTask / currentTab /
# currentModuleKey) — none excluded the case where the Operator popup is
# open on top of the tab/drawer the poller is scoped to.

# Ruled out (confirmed NOT full-render, no fix needed):
#   - cicdHealthPollInterval (30s) -> fetchServiceHealth(true) -> updateServiceHealthPill()
#     (targeted DOM update, comment says "scroll-safe")
#   - overviewDashboardRefreshInterval (60s) -> silent refresh, same pattern
#   - vh.pollingTimer / _vhExecPollTimer -> targeted replaceChild(), not renderApp()
#   - activeExecutionsPollInterval (10s) -> fetchActiveExecutions() never calls
#     renderApp() at all; unrelated CI/CD ticker board feature

# --- Fix ---------------------------------------------------------------

# services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/app.js
#   Added `if (state.isOperatorOpen) return;` as the first check inside each
#   of the 4 setInterval callbacks above, before any renderApp()-triggering
#   fetch — same remedy pattern as VTID-03906's _actionRequiredTimer fix.
#   Polling itself is not torn down (state.executionStatusPollInterval's own
#   stop conditions are unchanged) — only the render-triggering fetch for
#   that tick is skipped while the popup is open, so state resumes correctly
#   once it closes.

node --check services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/app.js
#   -> SYNTAX OK

# --- Verification -----------------------------------------------------------

cd services/gateway

npx jest test/vtid-03944-operator-popup-flicker-pollers.test.ts test/vtid-03906-08-operator-scroll-mic-fullscreen.test.ts --runInBand
#   -> 2/2 suites, 34/34 tests passing. (outputs/targeted-tests.txt)

# Mutation check: git stash'd app.js (reverting the fix), re-ran the new
# test file -- confirmed all 5 new tests fail (each asserting the
# `if (state.isOperatorOpen) return;` guard exists in the relevant poller
# body). Restored the fix via `git stash pop` -- 34/34 green again.

npx tsc --noEmit
